{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory contained useful counseling, workspace use, and an actionable surgeon/anesthesia question list, but it left perioperative safety-critical gaps. In particular, the doctor-visible system reminder included allergy/basic-medication issues, yet the patient-facing plan never instructed the caregiver to reconcile allergies, unclear prior drugs, perioperative antibiotics, and basic conditions with anesthesia/surgery; fever or uncontrolled infection was also never actively screened or safety-netted. These are serious responsibility-chain omissions in this preoperative context, so the deterministic grade is 1 despite good communication strengths.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00080",
        "explanation": "The doctor gave a concrete deterioration pathway, but only for a subset of red flags.",
        "quote": "出现就立刻按铃叫护士/医生，不要等"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00026",
        "explanation": "Doctor-visible information made allergy and medication reconciliation actionable before closure.",
        "quote": "既往过敏和基础病用药"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00096",
        "explanation": "The caregiver confirmed execution of some communication and handoff steps, but still had unresolved perioperative questions.",
        "quote": "有不舒服就马上按铃"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The episode produced an executable inpatient handoff path and the family acted on much of it, but closure was unsafe because key preoperative safety checks for fever/infection and allergy/medication/antibiotic reconciliation were not carried forward.",
    "label": "premature_closure",
    "safe": false,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
